From 71de3a18aed71a8968c07edd1fc1741f8fda5112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:47:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: a policy to render padded targets in place
 (PaddedTargetsPolicy)

A texture over a buffer whose rows lie with bytes between them, and which
renders or which a shader writes, is a shadow: its texels copied in before
each use and back after each write, as a render pass's loads and stores may
write back every byte of its subresource. A display's framebuffer is such a
texture wherever the surface's rows are wider than its texels (1125 pixels
at 4608 bytes), so every pass into it copied the whole surface in and out.
DevicePolicy::padded_targets keeps that by default (Shadow); Alias makes it
an image over the buffer's rows, as PaddedReadsPolicy::Alias does for one that
only reads, for a consumer that checked its driver leaves those bytes. The
ledger names it; it keys no profile; on lavapipe a padded target under Alias
is aliased where the device lays the pitch (5248, 1216, 7680, 5312) and
renders as its private twin with no shadow copy (the new lane test, run there
without the validation layer this WSL lacks). Every lib test as before.
